# K03 NS-ROLES-1 / NS-ROLES-VIS (the author, 2026-10-07; semantics #declaration-visibility): `b: A` binds b to an
# A visible where b stands -- an ordinary named Structure is visible from its place on, not above it.
# box and inner stand above Later: each defines a Structure of its own (with the free name Later), no binding --
# a write of their v names no field of theirs: refused (the method is checked first, at inner\v).
# (A positive while -07 Q2 stood: a write through box reached Later.)
box: Later
box\v: 5
fn: m () int
    if: Later\v != 5
        return: 81
    inner: Later
    inner\v: 6
    if: Later\v != 6
        return: 82
    return: 7
end: m
Later:
    int: v 1
end: Later
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
